- The player can fly away from the planet.
- Atmospheric layers transition naturally.
- The planet becomes visible as a globe.
- The player can enter space and return.
- Procedural space generation has no artificial terminal boundary.

**Animals**
- Animals face the direction in which they move.
- They do not walk sideways or backwards accidentally.
- They turn naturally.
- They have appropriate species-specific locomotion.
- Their feet make convincing ground contact.
- The third-person camera stays behind the creature.
